ecutive weeks.","thumbnail":"https:\u002F\u002Fresource.mistorebox.com\u002Finsights\u002Fcms_uploads\u002Fimg\u002Fdownload\u002Fbitcoin-explodes-02_Small.jpg","time":1794211497,"topType":"crypto-analysis","secondType":"bitcoin","route":"fxstreet-BTCUSDETHUSD-202611091604"},{"title":"Bitcoin ETFs sold $1.28 billion in a week — and BTC is still above 75,000","abstract":"US spot Bitcoin ETFs logged $1.28 billion of net outflows in the week to Nov 6, the largest since late June, with BlackRock's IBIT accounting for $1.21 billion. Yet BTC only fell from $80,405 to $74,940, a 6.8% move. The gap between the fund flow and the price is the story: leveraged longs were flushed, but spot holders did not follow the ETFs out — and $75,000 is the line that decides whether that reading holds.","thumbnail":"https:\u002F\u002Fresource.mistorebox.com\u002Finsights\u002Fcms_uploads\u002Fimg\u002F20231102\u002F11ffed3a9788fef29ed64dd5b2973fe0.jpg","time":1794193326,"topType":"crypto-analysis","secondType":"bitcoin","route":"bitcoin-etf-outflow-75000-20261109J1047"},{"title":"Binance replaced 95% of a $6.3bn hole — Bitcoin is trading the plumbing, not the coin","abstract":"Binance resumed withdrawals on November 1 after a record $6.3bn theft. In the first 9.5 hours, users withdrew $4.64bn and deposited $1.01bn, a net outflow of $3.64bn, or 2.1% of assets. Bitcoin fell to 76,173 and is now 78,473. The market is pricing the exchange, not the supply.","thumbnail":"https:\u002F\u002Fresource.mistorebox.com\u002Finsights\u002Fcms_uploads\u002Fimg\u002F20250604\u002F10face3f7ffa1150284f70c8a4386885.jpg","time":1793585895,"topType":"crypto-analysis","secondType":"bitcoin","route":"binance-63bn-hole-bitcoin-plumbing-20261102J1018"}],"type":"news\u002Fcrypto-analysis","value":"Cryptocurrency"}],"blog":[{"data":[{"title":"10 Best Day Trading Platforms for Beginners and Active Traders in 2026: A Practical Guide","abstract":"Best Day Trading Platforms for 2026: A Complete Guide for Retail Traders"